/salprod
-----------
OLD LUN: LUN_23
NEW LUN: 

On punifiart010:
- Freeze Artiva-Prod cluster group 
hagrp -freeze Artiva-Prod
- rescan bus to find new storage (/root/scripts/scan_*sh)
- write label with fdisk
fdisk <new device>
w
- initialize with Veritas vxdiskadm and add to metadg disk-group
vxdisk scandisks
vxdiskadm
- 1: initialize disk 
- default values except of "Name of disk", then choose later a name with LUN_173
- mirror /salprod to new disks with vxassist (vxassit -g <disk-group> mirror <volume-name> alloc=<new name>)
vxassist -g metadg mirror salprod alloc=LUN_X
- mirror /journal to new disks with vxassist (vxassit -g <disk-group> mirror <volume-name> alloc=<new name>)

- Wait for first SplitMirrorBackupArtiva.sh SyncDisk started for this server
- remove old mirror with vxassist (vxassist -g <disk-group> remove mirror <volume name> \!<old name>)
- - Make sure you run this command when the BCVs to the old LUN are not fractured (so they're synchronized or synchrozing). This is very important to avoid a split-brain situation on the backup server punififac330
vxassist -g metadg remove mirror salprod \!LUN_23 

- Grow logival volume (vxassist -g <disk-group> maxgrow <volume name> alloc=<diskname where volume lives on>)
vxassist -g metadg maxgrow salprod alloc=LUN_X 
these commands get you the maximum size of volume, note it
- increase logical volume and filesystem with vxresize (/usr/lib/vxvm/bin/vxresize -g <disk-group> <volume name> <max new size> alloc=<diskname where volume lives on>)
/usr/lib/vxvm/bin/vxresize -g metadg salprod <max new size> alloc=LUN_X

- Remove old disk from Veritas
vxdg -g metadg rmdisk LUN_23

#vxdisk offline emcpowere
#vxdisk rm emcpowere
#powermt remove dev=emcpowere

On punifiart030:
- Scan for new storage (/root/scripts/scan_*)
- Let VxVM scan for new storage (vxdisk scandisks)
- Make sure it sees the new storage and it's in the correct diskgroup (vxdisk -o alldgs scandisks)
- Unfreeze cluster service group
hagrp -unfreeze Artiva-Prod

On punifiart020:
- rescan bus to find new storage (/root/scripts/scan_*.sh)
- Edit /usr/local/scripts/CloneLst.txt and change device name, LUN, and ClonedLUN
- Make sure new BCV is in same state than other LUNs. 
- - If they're split, then split it also
- - If they're synchronized or synchronizing, start this process also with 
- - - /opt/VRTSjre/jre1.4/bin/java -jar /opt/Navisphere/bin/navicli.jar -User facsclone -Password <password> -Scope 0 -address clardsk24spa snapview -syncclone -name <New BCV clone group name> -cloneid 0100000000000000 -o


Verify that new filesystem got imported and mounted correctly

Open change request to SAN team (CSC SAN Storage.Remove) to remove the old LUN.


